  "narrative": "In the 2020s, Black and African women's hairstyles continue to be a vibrant expression of their cultural heritage and identity. The afro remains a popular style, showcasing natural growth and texture with its distinctive curl pattern. Protective styles like box braids and cornrows are also favored for their ability to minimize hair breakage and promote healthy hair growth. These styles not only protect the hair but also serve as a means of self-expression and cultural connection. The natural hair movement continues to gain momentum, encouraging individuals to celebrate and embrace their Afro-textured hair. Dreadlocks and locs have also become increasingly popular, with some women opting for this hairstyle as a way to showcase their unique texture and style. While the source material does not provide specific documentation on hairstyles during the 2020s, it is clear that Black and African women's hair culture remains a dynamic and expressive aspect of their identity.",
